GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf
# GitPython <= 3.1.57, fixed in 3.1.58: five ways to smuggle unsafe options or
# attacker-chosen names into git — option forwarding in `IndexFile.from_tree`,
# `Repo.init(template=…)` hooks, unvalidated `.gitmodules` section names,
# git-config option-name injection, and a bypass of the unsafe-option guard.
# Every one of them needs Open WebUI to run a git operation on input someone
# else chose. This deployment sets OFFLINE_MODE (no update checks, no external
# APIs), keeps chat file upload off and binds the UI to loopback, so there is
# no path here that clones or rewrites a repository on request. Exit: the next
# image built on 3.1.58. Added 2026-08-08.
GHSA-4gmw-gg2m-w46p
GHSA-9rj7-rf2p-w77r
GHSA-hmq2-w58f-27jc
GHSA-jm78-9fvv-mhgr
GHSA-wvpp-8hx9-p66j
# pymdown-extensions <= 11.0.0, fixed in 11.0.1: exponential backtracking in
# four inline processors, so one crafted Markdown line under 50 bytes burns
# CPU on the rendering thread. The Markdown reaching it here is the operator's
# own messages and their local model's output on a single-user loopback stack:
# the worst case is hanging your own container, not a shared service. Exit:
# the next image built on 11.0.1. Added 2026-08-08.
CVE-2026-67422

# --- qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0 (latest release) ---------------------------------
# Dashboard npm dependencies, Rust crates (pyo3, quinn-proto) and tar. Qdrant
# publishes no host port; access goes through Reed's API or
# `docker compose exec`. Entries carried over from v1.18.3 — any the bump
# fixed are inert (ignoring an absent finding is a no-op) and get pruned on
# the next reviewed rescan.
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-59869
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-69152
GHSA-36hh-v3qg-5jq4
GHSA-4w2j-m93h-cj5j
GHSA-gcfj-64vw-6mp9
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849
# js-yaml < 4.3.1 in the dashboard's npm tree: quadratic CPU burn parsing a
# crafted !!omap YAML. Exploiting it means making the dashboard parse
# attacker YAML — and the dashboard is reachable only from the stack's own
# network (no host port, loopback-only deployment). The fix landed in
# js-yaml 4.3.1 on 2026-08-06, one day after v1.19.0 was cut, so no qdrant
# image carries it yet; the weekly rescan and the next qdrant release are
# this entry's exit path. Added 2026-08-07.
GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj
# nanoid in the same dashboard tree: an infinite loop in customAlphabet and
# customRandom when the size is zero (CVE-2026-67213, fixed in 3.3.17/5.1.6),
# and in the non-secure generator when the size is negative (CVE-2026-67214,
# fixed in 3.3.16/5.1.16). Both need the caller to pass a size the dashboard
# never takes from input, and the dashboard has no published port either way.
# Exit: the next qdrant release. Added 2026-08-08.
CVE-2026-67213
CVE-2026-67214

